# Generated validation evidence. These receipts are rewritten on every run and
# contain machine-specific data (window station/desktop names, install paths).
# Committing them would change `git status` on each run, which is part of the
# staging manifest's `repositoryStatusLines` source identity, and would make
# restage + build fail with "Runtime manifest source identity changed".
# Durable evidence belongs in a release receipt or .local/, not in source.
platform/windows-tsf/validation/*/runs/

# Browser-automation scratch output from tooling that drives a real browser
# (page snapshots and console logs). Same reasoning as the entries above: it is
# rewritten on every run and would otherwise make `git status` dirty, which is
# part of the staging manifest's repositoryStatusLines source identity.
.playwright-mcp/
